<p>This Policy explains how we collect, use, store, disclose and protect personal information when you visit Nestyroo, subscribe to our newsletter or contact us. Our website is intended primarily for an Australian audience but may be accessed from other countries. We handle personal information in accordance with laws that apply to our activities.</p>
<p>The EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) may apply to our processing of personal data. The Australian Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and Australian Privacy Principles may also apply depending on the circumstances. Mentioning a law does not mean every provision necessarily applies to every visitor or activity.</p>
<p>Official legislation: GDPR - <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj" rel="noopener">https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj</a></p>
<p>Australian Privacy Act 1988 - <a href="https://www.legislation.gov.au/C2004A03712/latest/text" rel="noopener">https://www.legislation.gov.au/C2004A03712/latest/text</a></p>
<h2 id="information-we-collect">2. Information we collect</h2>
<h3 id="information-you-provide">2.1 Information you provide</h3>
<p>Newsletter subscriptions: first name, email address, optional interest categories, and the date, source and status of your subscription and consent where recorded. The newsletter is intended only for people aged 18 or older. Subscription is optional.</p>
<p>Contact and enquiry forms: your name, email address, message and information you choose to include in a question, complaint, partnership or other enquiry. Please do not submit sensitive personal information unless necessary for your enquiry.</p>
<h3 id="technical-and-usage-information">2.2 Technical and usage information</h3>
<p>Our hosting provider and analytics tools may process technical information such as browser and device information, pages viewed, referral information, website interactions, request dates and times, and technical information relating to website operation, performance and security. Netlify, our hosting provider, may process visitors' IP addresses as part of its hosting and server-log operations. Google Analytics 4 (GA4), as configured on our website, does not log or store visitors' IP addresses.</p>
<p>We do not intentionally ask GA4 to collect your name or email address. Technical identifiers and usage data may nevertheless qualify as personal data under applicable laws.</p>
<h3 id="technical-server-logs">2.3 Technical server logs</h3>
<p>When visitors access Nestyroo, our hosting provider, Netlify, automatically generates technical server logs as part of providing and maintaining the website. These logs may contain information such as IP addresses, country information, access timestamps, browser and device details, and technical request information.</p>
<p>This information is processed for purposes including website delivery, security, troubleshooting, abuse prevention and service reliability. Netlify determines the applicable retention periods for its technical server logs under its operational policies. Nestyroo does not directly control or configure the retention period of these hosting logs.</p>
<h3 id="features-not-currently-provided">2.4 Features not currently provided</h3>
<p>Nestyroo does not currently provide visitor accounts, public comments, visitor uploads or public review-submission features. We do not currently process personal information through those features.</p>
<p>We do not sell or rent visitors' personal information, and do not knowingly exchange personal information for money or provide it to third parties for their independent marketing purposes.</p>
<h2 id="purposes-of-processing">3. Purposes of processing</h2>
<p>We use personal information to administer newsletter subscriptions; send newsletter communications that subscribers have agreed to receive; respond to questions, complaints and partnership enquiries; host, deliver, maintain and troubleshoot the website; understand website usage and improve content and usability; identify technical issues and protect the website; maintain necessary records; and comply with legal obligations or establish, exercise or defend legal claims.</p>
<p>We do not use newsletter or contact-form information for unrelated purposes incompatible with the purpose for which it was collected.</p>
<h2 id="legal-bases-under-the-gdpr">4. Legal bases under the GDPR</h2>
<p>Where the GDPR applies, we rely on the legal basis appropriate to each activity:</p>
<p>Consent (GDPR Article 6(1)(a)): newsletter marketing and analytics cookies or similar technologies where consent is required and is the basis used.</p>
<p>Legitimate interests (Article 6(1)(f)): where appropriate, to administer enquiries, maintain website security, prevent abuse, keep essential operational records and improve the website, after considering the impact on individuals and their rights.</p>
<p>Legal obligation (Article 6(1)(c)): where processing is necessary to comply with a legal obligation.</p>
<p>Contract or pre-contractual steps (Article 6(1)(b)): where applicable to a specific request made by you. We do not assume every general enquiry creates a contract.</p>
<p>Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw it at any time; withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing before withdrawal. You may object to processing based on legitimate interests where the GDPR provides that right.</p>
<h2 id="newsletter-and-marketing">5. Newsletter and marketing</h2>
<p>Newsletter subscriptions are optional. We intend to use subscription details to administer the subscription and send the newsletter or related communications covered by the subscriber's consent. We do not sell or rent the newsletter list or share it with unrelated businesses for their own marketing.</p>
<p>All newsletter sign-up forms are intended for people aged 18 or older and require an active consent choice. Before sending marketing emails, we will use an email delivery provider and configure the process to include appropriate sender identification, contact details and an unsubscribe method. The provider may process subscriber information on our behalf. We have not yet selected that provider; this Policy will be updated if needed to reflect material changes.</p>
<p>You can unsubscribe using the method provided in a marketing email, where available, or by emailing <a href="mailto:privacy@nestyroo.com">privacy@nestyroo.com</a>. We will process unsubscribe requests within the period required by applicable law.</p>
<h3 id="newsletter-data-retention">Newsletter data retention</h3>
<p>Newsletter registration information is reviewed at least quarterly. Registrations that have reached 24 months from the original sign-up date are deleted during the next quarterly review, unless a longer retention period is required by applicable law.</p>
<p>If a subscriber unsubscribes, we delete their other newsletter registration information and retain only the minimum information necessary, such as their email address and the date of their unsubscribe request, on a separate suppression list. This limited record is retained for as long as necessary to respect their unsubscribe preference and prevent them from being inadvertently added to future mailing lists.</p>
<p>If a person subsequently chooses to subscribe again, they must complete the newsletter sign-up form and actively provide consent again. We treat this as a new subscription and record the new consent details. Where fresh consent is provided, the suppression status will be updated to reflect the new subscription, while retaining an appropriate record of the new consent.</p>
<p>Consent records are retained while the related subscriber information is held and where otherwise necessary to demonstrate compliance.</p>
<h2 id="contact-forms-and-enquiries">6. Contact forms and enquiries</h2>
<p>We use information submitted through contact forms to respond to and manage the relevant enquiry. Our intended retention period is approximately 12 months after the enquiry is resolved, unless longer retention is necessary for an ongoing matter, a legal obligation, security or the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims.</p>
<p>Privacy requests: <a href="mailto:privacy@nestyroo.com">privacy@nestyroo.com</a></p>
<p>Complaints and legal enquiries: <a href="mailto:complaints@nestyroo.com">complaints@nestyroo.com</a></p>
<p>General questions: <a href="mailto:hello@nestyroo.com">hello@nestyroo.com</a></p>
<h2 id="cookies-local-storage-and-analytics">7. Cookies, local storage and analytics</h2>
<p>Nestyroo uses Google Analytics 4 (GA4) to understand website usage, subject to the visitor's consent where required. The website also uses browser local storage to remember when a visitor dismisses the newsletter pop-up and to remember their cookie consent choice. These technologies help the website remember visitor preferences. Cookies and local storage are different technologies and may store identifiers, consent choices or preference information in your browser.</p>
<p>GA4 may use cookies or similar technologies and may process online identifiers and usage data. We do not intentionally use GA4 to collect your name or email address.</p>
<p>Where consent is legally required for analytics cookies or similar technologies, we request consent before those technologies are activated. Visitors can reject non-essential analytics without being prevented from accessing ordinary website content.</p>
<p>Visitors can change or withdraw their analytics consent at any time using the 'Cookie settings' link available in the website footer. Where consent is withdrawn, analytics cookies are removed and further analytics tracking is stopped. Browser settings can also be used to manage cookies, although disabling some technologies may affect functionality.</p>
<p>The technologies actually loaded, timing of analytics activation and available consent controls determine whether the website meets applicable requirements. This Policy does not replace the need for those controls to work as described.</p>
<p>The EU ePrivacy Directive 2002/58/EC, as amended, may be relevant where applicable: <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32002L0058" rel="noopener">https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32002L0058</a></p>
<h2 id="service-providers-and-recipients">8. Service providers and recipients</h2>
<p>Netlify - website hosting and forms. Netlify hosts the website and stores submissions made through its forms. It may process technical information and server logs, including IP addresses, to deliver and secure the service. Form submissions and logs are subject to applicable service configuration and retention settings.</p>
<p>Google Analytics 4 - analytics. Google provides analytics services to help us understand website usage. Google may process technical identifiers and usage information under applicable Google terms, privacy documentation and our configuration.</p>
<p>GitHub - code and content. GitHub is used to store and manage website code and related project content. We do not use GitHub as a visitor database or intentionally submit visitor form data to it.</p>
<p>Decap CMS - internal content editing. Decap CMS is used by our team to manage website content. It is not a visitor account service; visitors do not need a Decap CMS account to use Nestyroo.</p>
<p>Future email provider. When selected, the provider may process subscriber details on our behalf. We will update this Policy if needed to reflect material changes.</p>
<p>We do not currently identify any other separate security or monitoring service beyond those described above. If our service providers change, we will update this Policy where appropriate.</p>
<h2 id="affiliate-links-and-third-party-websites">9. Affiliate links and third-party websites</h2>
<p>Nestyroo does not currently use active affiliate links. We may introduce affiliate links or other advertising arrangements in the future. If introduced, these may generate revenue for Nestyroo, and relevant disclosures will be provided.</p>
<p>If affiliate links are introduced, they may contain tracking identifiers that help an affiliate network or retailer attribute a visit or purchase to Nestyroo. Clicking an affiliate link takes you to a third-party website. That website or its affiliate network may use cookies or similar technologies under its own privacy and cookie practices. Nestyroo does not itself set third-party affiliate cookies on the retailer's website and does not control the retailer's independent data processing.</p>
<p>We do not receive your full payment details through affiliate links. Purchases, payments, deliveries and returns are handled by the relevant retailer, not Nestyroo. Affiliate relationships will be disclosed in relevant content. Review the third party's privacy policy before providing information or making a purchase.</p>
<h2 id="international-processing-and-transfers">10. International processing and transfers</h2>
<p>Nestyroo uses third-party service providers that may store, access or process personal information outside Bulgaria and the European Economic Area (EEA), including in the United States.</p>
<p>In particular:</p>
<ul>
<li><p><strong>Netlify:</strong> Our website hosting and form-processing provider, Netlify, processes and stores contact-form submissions and newsletter registration information in the United States. Netlify may also engage subprocessors located in the United States and other countries to provide its services.</p></li>
<li><p><strong>Google Analytics 4:</strong> Where a visitor has provided the required consent, Google Analytics may process website usage information internationally in accordance with Google's applicable data-processing arrangements.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>Where personal information is transferred outside the EEA, we rely on an applicable legal transfer mechanism under data protection law. Depending on the recipient and the transfer concerned, this may include an adequacy decision, such as the EU-US Data Privacy Framework where the recipient is appropriately certified and the transfer is covered, or appropriate safeguards such as Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs).</p>
<p>Further information about the relevant providers, their subprocessors and their data-protection arrangements is available through their respective privacy policies and data-processing documentation.</p>
<p>If Australian privacy law applies to a particular activity, we will address relevant cross-border disclosure obligations under that law.</p>
<h2 id="retention">11. Retention</h2>
<p>We keep personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Policy, subject to applicable legal requirements.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Newsletter registrations: reviewed at least quarterly and deleted during the next quarterly review after reaching 24 months from the original sign-up date (see section 5).</p></li>
<li><p>Newsletter consent records: while related subscriber information is held and where otherwise necessary to demonstrate consent.</p></li>
<li><p>Unsubscribed subscribers: a minimal suppression record (email address and unsubscribe date) is retained for as long as necessary to honour the request and prevent unwanted marketing.</p></li>
<li><p>Contact messages: approximately 12 months after the enquiry is resolved, unless a longer period is justified.</p></li>
<li><p>Technical server logs: for the period determined by Netlify, which Nestyroo does not directly control (see section 2.3). We do not keep separate copies of these logs.</p></li>
<li><p>Google Analytics data: GA4 user-level and event-level data is subject to a 14-month retention period under our current configuration. The setting to reset the retention period on new activity is disabled.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>Retention may be longer where necessary to resolve a dispute, comply with law, maintain security or establish, exercise or defend legal claims. We will not retain personal data indefinitely merely because it was once collected.</p>
<h2 id="security">12. Security</h2>
<p>We use reasonable technical and organisational measures intended to protect personal information from unauthorised access, loss, misuse, alteration or disclosure. These include using service providers for hosting and forms and restricting access to information to those who need it for website operations. No website, transmission method or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>
<p>If a personal data breach occurs, we will take the steps required by applicable law, including any required notifications.</p>
<h2 id="your-privacy-rights">13. Your privacy rights</h2>
<p>Depending on your location and the laws that apply, you may have rights to request access to personal data; request correction or deletion; request restriction of processing; object to certain processing; withdraw consent where processing is based on consent; receive a portable copy of certain information where provided by law; and complain to a relevant privacy or data protection regulator. These rights are subject to applicable conditions and exceptions.</p>
<p>To exercise a right, email <a href="mailto:privacy@nestyroo.com">privacy@nestyroo.com</a> and explain your request. We may ask for reasonable information to verify your identity and locate relevant records. We will respond within the period required by applicable law.</p>
<p>If the GDPR applies, you may complain to a competent supervisory authority, including the authority in your place of habitual residence, place of work or the place of an alleged infringement, where applicable. AppricotAds LTD is established in Bulgaria; the Bulgarian Commission for Personal Data Protection website is <a href="https://www.cpdp.bg/" rel="noopener">https://www.cpdp.bg/</a>.</p>
<p>For Australian visitors, we aim to handle personal information transparently and responsibly and seek to follow practices consistent with the Australian Privacy Principles where appropriate. This is a statement of intended practices, not a formal opt-in to the Australian Privacy Act and not a determination that the Act applies to every activity. If the Act applies, the relevant legal requirements govern.</p>
<h2 id="children">14. Children</h2>
<p>Nestyroo's newsletter and contact forms are intended only for people aged 18 or older. The forms require an age confirmation. We do not knowingly accept newsletter subscriptions or contact-form submissions from anyone under 18. The website's general informational content is not intended to encourage children to provide personal information. If you believe a person under 18 has submitted information, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@nestyroo.com">privacy@nestyroo.com</a> so we can review the matter and take appropriate action.</p>
<h2 id="changes-to-this-policy">15. Changes to this Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Policy when our practices, services or legal obligations change. The latest version will be published on Nestyroo with an updated &quot;Last updated&quot; date. If a change materially affects how we process information, we will take any notification or consent steps required by applicable law.</p>
